@presidential_candidate_left_incumbent
title: Run President [+ president +], the incumbent.
subtitle: The incumbency may give us an advantage over fielding a new candidate.
view-if: president == "Crispien" or president == "Levi" or president == "Sender" or president == "Rosenfeld" or president == "Seydewitz" or president == "Siemsen"
on-arrival: {!
left_campaign = 1;
if (president == "Crispien") {
    spd_presidential_candidate = "Crispien";
} else if (president == "Levi") {
    spd_presidential_candidate = "Levi";
} else if (president == "Sender") {
    spd_presidential_candidate = "Sender";
} else if (president == "Rosenfeld") {
    spd_presidential_candidate = "Rosenfeld";
} else if (president == "Seydewitz") {
    spd_presidential_candidate = "Seydewitz";
} else if (president == "Siemsen") {
    spd_presidential_candidate = "Siemsen";
}
!}

We have made the incumbent President [+ spd_presidential_candidate +] our candidate for the upcoming Presidential elections.

- @spd_presidential_campaign: Now onto the campaign

@presidential_candidate_left_previous
title: Run [+ spd_presidential_candidate +], our candidate at the last election.
subtitle: Their high profile from the previous campaign may give us an advantage.
view-if: (chancellor != "Crispien" and president != "Crispien" and spd_presidential_candidate  == "Crispien") or (chancellor != "Levi" and president != "Levi" and spd_presidential_candidate  == "Levi") or (chancellor != "Sender" and president != "Sender" and spd_presidential_candidate  == "Sender") or (chancellor != "Rosenfeld" and president != "Rosenfeld" and spd_presidential_candidate  == "Rosenfeld") or (chancellor != "Seydewitz" and president != "Seydewitz" and spd_presidential_candidate  == "Seydewitz") or (chancellor != "Siemsen" and president != "Siemsen" and spd_presidential_candidate  == "Siemsen") 
on-arrival: left_campaign = 1

- @spd_presidential_campaign: Now onto the campaign
    
@presidential_candidate_left_chancellor
Title: Run our Chancellor [+ chancellor +] 
subtitle: Their high profile from Chancellorship may give us an advantage. They will have to resign the Chancellorship if they win, however.
view-if: chancellor == "Crispien" or chancellor == "Levi" or chancellor == "Sender" or chancellor == "Rosenfeld" or chancellor == "Seydewitz" or chancellor == "Siemsen"
on-arrival: {!
    left_campaign = 1;
    if (chancellor == "Crispien") {
        spd_presidential_candidate = "Crispien";
    } else if (chancellor == "Levi") {
        spd_presidential_candidate = "Levi";
    } else if (chancellor == "Sender") {
        spd_presidential_candidate = "Sender";
    } else if (chancellor == "Rosenfeld") {
        spd_presidential_candidate = "Rosenfeld";
    } else if (chancellor == "Seydewitz") {
        spd_presidential_candidate = "Seydewitz";
    } else if (chancellor == "Siemsen") {
        spd_presidential_candidate = "Siemsen";
    }
!}

We have made Chancellor [+ spd_presidential_candidate +] our candidate for the upcoming Presidential elections. 

- @spd_presidential_campaign: Now onto the campaign

